@startuml
title KTOB — System Use Case Model (R1)
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
actor Reader
actor "Open Library API" as Catalog <<external>>
actor "AI Provider" as AI <<external>>
actor "Seller Research Source" as Sellers <<unconfirmed>>
rectangle "KTOB" {
 usecase "Sign in / register" as UCAuth
 usecase "Manage profile, consent\nand content boundaries" as UCPrivacy
 usecase "Search / discover a book" as UCSearch
 usecase "Manually enter a book" as UCManual
 usecase "Add work to library" as UCLibrary
 usecase "Manage reading status\nand favorites" as UCStatus
 usecase "Manage collections" as UCCollections
 usecase "Record / reread a book" as UCRead
 usecase "Write private reflections" as UCJournal
 usecase "Discuss a book\nor literature" as UCChat
 usecase "Review proposed AI memory" as UCMemory
 usecase "Request recommendations" as UCRecommend
 usecase "Find a copy" as UCFind
 usecase "Save seller offer" as UCSave
 usecase "Record acquisition" as UCAcquire
 usecase "Export personal records" as UCExport
 usecase "Use permitted personal context" as UCContext
 usecase "Apply boundaries" as UCBound
}
Reader --> UCAuth
Reader --> UCPrivacy
Reader --> UCSearch
Reader --> UCLibrary
Reader --> UCStatus
Reader --> UCCollections
Reader --> UCRead
Reader --> UCJournal
Reader --> UCChat
Reader --> UCMemory
Reader --> UCRecommend
Reader --> UCFind
Reader --> UCSave
Reader --> UCAcquire
Reader --> UCExport
UCManual ..> UCSearch : <<extend>>\nwhen not found
UCLibrary ..> UCSearch : <<include>>
UCRecommend ..> UCBound : <<include>>
UCRecommend ..> UCContext : <<extend>>\nonly after opt-in
UCChat ..> UCContext : <<extend>>\nonly after opt-in
UCMemory ..> UCChat : <<extend>>\nreader approval
UCSave ..> UCFind : <<extend>>\noptional
UCAcquire ..> UCFind : <<extend>>\noptional and explicit
Catalog --> UCSearch
AI --> UCChat
AI --> UCRecommend
Sellers --> UCFind
note right of UCAcquire
No acquisition inferred from seller visit.
No reading status implied by acquisition.
end note
note bottom of UCPrivacy
Each user's data is private.
Personalization defaults to off.
end note
@enduml
